{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1466811-forced-disappearance-technocracy-tactic-normalization-versus-conspicuousness","id":1466811,"title":"Forced Disappearance... Technocracy Tactic, Normalization versus Conspicuousness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-05T13:12:15-07:00","id":1466811,"title":"Forced Disappearance... Technocracy Tactic, Normalization versus Conspicuousness","content":"Forced Disappearance is kidnapping of a person by their own government (usually) or by a foreign government. The Technocracy operates within government institutions and uses this tactic. You are either playing characters who look over their shoulder for vehicles with tinted windows or you may potentially have to carry out such orders. No matter how well executed the kidnapping, the absence of the person is something that people notice and talk about. In the digital age, sleepers have tools with which they can investigate. <br /> <br /> My Chronicle is set in the United States and I suspect most people's Chronicles are set in The West, but don't let my west-centric bias limit the scope of the discussion. Wikipedia lists examples of countries where this has happened or continues to happen: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forced_disappearance\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forced_disappearance</a><br /> <br /> In my view, if it is common, then there is going to be some kind of organized effort to investigate official government perpetrators (like by Amnesty International), but is less conspicuous for Mage Kidnappers - more Coincidental, since it is somewhat normalized. <br /> <br /> I also think that if it is uncommon, there might not be any organized effort to investigate the practice, but Mage Kidnappers might have greater difficulty pulling it off, depending how they do it. <br /> <br /> How conspicuous is this tactic?<br /> <br /> How do you investigate it, as a Mage? <br /> <br /> How do you pull it off?<br /> <br /> What social conditions make it easier to carry out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T14:44:00-07:00","id":1466820,"title":"","content":"I think one of the Union's biggest advantages here, is that most mages (even their own) live on the fringes of society because they don't want to be tracked easily. Most mages want to be able to disappear if they have to, and thus avoid situations where them being gone for a week or two would make anyone think something was up (or at least by those that would make a stink about it publicly).<br /> <br /> ~540,000 people went missing in the USA last year. The vast majority of those cases never get significant new coverage, investigations by public or private organizations, etc. The Technocrats rolling up to your house where lots of Sleeper cameras might see what's going on to grab you in the middle of the night and toss you into a black van? That's going to be something the Union avoids. If they can just wait for you to go on a regular hiking or camping trip to take you? Well then you're just one of the thousands of people that got lost in the woods never to be found; and they easily have lots of time to cover up any lingering evidence (and even block magical investigations if they feel like it).<br /> <br /> Mages are, by their position in the world, masters of thinking about how things look to everyone else. They're going to invariably orient towards tactics that take advantage of public apathy (or worse). Overt forced disappearances are too flashy for how mags tend to think. It's also frequently impractical (raiding a mage in their home could easily mean dealing with a Sanctum, changing the Reality dynamics and having a whole slew of magical traps to deal with). So just like it's easier to coincidentally make a gun that performs really well than it is to throw fireballs at people, mages looking to kidnap other mages are going to look for things that don't rile suspicions.<br /> <br /> Investigating what happened to your fellow mage that suddenly disappeared is pretty situational. Technocrats don't talk about other agents that were angling for reeducation suddenly disappearing unless they want to be next. Nephandi frequently throw each other under the bus, and would take the change to pin their own misdeeds on a captured Nephandus than worry about who took them. Orphans and smaller Crafts probably have to resign themselves to not pressing investigations past a certain point because... what are they going to really do once they trace things back to a more powerful group of mages?<br /> <br /> Even with the larger Crafts, the Disparate Alliance, the Traditions, and the Union dealing with external threats, magic makes any generalities about how investigations will go difficult to make. What Spheres and skills are brought to bear by each side matter a lot.<br /> <br /> One thing basically doesn't change from the real world, to the WoD, to mages specifically: getting away with it is not about nobody finding out. It's about making the cost of investigation and the cost of fighting for the victim's freedom so high that people either give up or grind themselves futilely at the effort until whatever reason you had for kidnapping in the first place is fulfilled and it doesn't really matter any more. A dedicated mage that wants to find out what happened to their friend will, eventually, find out. Doing it before the Union has already extracted all the intel they wanted out of their target's mind, and then used disposable Sleeper agents to deal with the body as the only people our intrepid investigator can get revenge on... why would the Union care if they're eventually implicated?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T17:54:04-07:00","id":1466844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1466811-forced-disappearance-technocracy-tactic-normalization-versus-conspicuousness?p=1466820#post1466820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of the Union's biggest advantages here, is that most mages (even their own) live on the fringes of society because they don't want to be tracked easily. Most mages want to be able to disappear if they have to, and thus avoid situations where them being gone for a week or two would make anyone think something was up (or at least by those that would make a stink about it publicly).<br /> <br /> ~540,000 people went missing in the USA last year. The vast majority of those cases never get significant new coverage, investigations by public or private organizations, etc. The Technocrats rolling up to your house where lots of Sleeper cameras might see what's going on to grab you in the middle of the night and toss you into a black van? That's going to be something the Union avoids. If they can just wait for you to go on a regular hiking or camping trip to take you? Well then you're just one of the thousands of people that got lost in the woods never to be found; and they easily have lots of time to cover up any lingering evidence (and even block magical investigations if they feel like it).</div> </div> </div> </div>If Union Operatives would be deterred from kidnapping by a Mage living in a populated area, wouldn't more Mages chose this over life on the fringes of society? You can more easily spread your influence in the city and there are group wilderness activities one could join or lead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1466811-forced-disappearance-technocracy-tactic-normalization-versus-conspicuousness?p=1466820#post1466820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages are, by their position in the world, masters of thinking about how things look to everyone else. They're going to invariably orient towards tactics that take advantage of public apathy (or worse). Overt forced disappearances are too flashy for how mags tend to think. It's also frequently impractical (raiding a mage in their home could easily mean dealing with a Sanctum, changing the Reality dynamics and having a whole slew of magical traps to deal with). So just like it's easier to coincidentally make a gun that performs really well than it is to throw fireballs at people, mages looking to kidnap other mages are going to look for things that don't rile suspicions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your logic is sensible here. Watch that pressure plate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1466811-forced-disappearance-technocracy-tactic-normalization-versus-conspicuousness?p=1466820#post1466820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Investigating what happened to your fellow mage that suddenly disappeared is pretty situational. Technocrats don't talk about other agents that were angling for reeducation suddenly disappearing unless they want to be next. Nephandi frequently throw each other under the bus, and would take the change to pin their own misdeeds on a captured Nephandus than worry about who took them. Orphans and smaller Crafts probably have to resign themselves to not pressing investigations past a certain point because... what are they going to really do once they trace things back to a more powerful group of mages?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that in one book featured on Mage The Podcast, Orphan Cabals would allow their own to be prostituted to wealthy sleepers who sometimes murder them and throw them down a corpse disposal shaft, I guess Orphans wouldn't even bother to look in the first place. I'm not necessarily talking about how people actually play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1466811-forced-disappearance-technocracy-tactic-normalization-versus-conspicuousness?p=1466820#post1466820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with the larger Crafts, the Disparate Alliance, the Traditions, and the Union dealing with external threats, magic makes any generalities about how investigations will go difficult to make. What Spheres and skills are brought to bear by each side matter a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>In larger organizations, Mages can network to find others with the appropriate Spheres, which I think would be Correspondence 2 and Time 2.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1466811-forced-disappearance-technocracy-tactic-normalization-versus-conspicuousness?p=1466820#post1466820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing basically doesn't change from the real world, to the WoD, to mages specifically: getting away with it is not about nobody finding out. It's about making the cost of investigation and the cost of fighting for the victim's freedom so high that people either give up or grind themselves futilely at the effort until whatever reason you had for kidnapping in the first place is fulfilled and it doesn't really matter any more. A dedicated mage that wants to find out what happened to their friend will, eventually, find out. Doing it before the Union has already extracted all the intel they wanted out of their target's mind, and then used disposable Sleeper agents to deal with the body as the only people our intrepid investigator can get revenge on... why would the Union care if they're eventually implicated?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's easier to build a missile that can destroy a Construct than it is to build a Construct. I could even imagine an Orphan going, &quot;Fuck those bastards! Titanium or not, I will knock that shit down.&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 11-05-2021, 09:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T18:41:44-07:00","id":1466849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1466811-forced-disappearance-technocracy-tactic-normalization-versus-conspicuousness?p=1466844#post1466844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Union Operatives would be deterred from kidnapping by a Mage living in a populated area, wouldn't more Mages chose this over life on the fringes of society? You can more easily spread your influence in the city and there are group wilderness activities one could join or lead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Change isn't always that simple for mages to do. A Dreamspeaker that regularly needs to deal with the Gauntlet is going to want to have places to go to with low Gauntlet ratings... which means far away from highly developed areas. Having a cult that has been indoctrinated into your paradigm generally requires a certain amount of isolation form general society to upkeep. Etc. Just being more urban and so on has its own costs for many mages.<br /> <br /> Also, I didn't mean to suggest that going off to the woods is the only option here. A mage that uses a rehab clinic to get away from people for a month isn't running off into the woods, but is providing their enemies a way to hide a forced disappearance. &quot;Local band's guitarist checks into rehab, disappears after seeming to leave the facility to meet with a dealer,&quot; is the kind of thing that is very easy to avoid a lot of public scrutiny over. Likewise, &quot;Minor YouTube inventor/streamer missing after a huge explosion at his lab on the edge of town,&quot; is an easy narrative to keep at least the Sleepers from digging into a Technocrat getting kidnapped.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Considering that in one book featured on Mage The Podcast, Orphan Cabals would allow their own Awakened to be prostituted to wealthy sleepers who sometimes murder them and throw them down a corpse disposal shaft, I guess Orphans wouldn't even bother to look in the first place. I'm talking about the book, not necessarily how people actually play. </div> </div> </div>Orphans are all unique. That specific cabal isn't how all Orphans, in the books, operate. Even that cabal would investigate on some level if someone was messing with their business. Viewing people as disposable assets doesn't mean you want other people stealing them from you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In larger organizations, Mages can network to find others with the appropriate Spheres, which I think would be Correspondence 2 and Time 2. </div> </div> </div>It would be enough (maybe Corr 3, Corr 2 lets you project your senses to where someone else is, but you might need 3 if that doesn't get you enough information)... if the other side isn't using magic to prevent being tracked. Scrying can be blocked, and warding against it is common enough among mages that it's hardly definitive to find a warded location. Time magic can get complicated. Lots of mages trying to view the same point in the past interfere with each other; which you can use to &quot;spike&quot; a moment in time and make it too fuzzy to see what was happening then.<br /> <br /> And of course, there's the &quot;see what happened when they got kidnapped,&quot; or, &quot;see where they are now,&quot; is frequently not enough to simply solve the issues when the other people have magic too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's easier to build a missile that can destroy a Construct than it is to build a Construct. I could even imagine an Orphan going, &quot;Fuck those bastards! Titanium or not, I will knock that shit down.&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Magic isn't quite as slanted in the favor of destruction as mundane technology is.<br /> <br /> And that still require said Orphan to find the Construct instead of finding the house of a Sleeper wetwork agent.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T19:01:53-07:00","id":1466852,"title":"","content":"Not to say that destroying the Construct with your friend inside may not be what said friend regards as &quot;rescue&quot;.<br /> <br /> It stands that the point is to make the cost as insurmountable as possible. If you're really driven to do something, you're likely to achieve it, at least in its simplest form. But until you do so, they had the time to do their thing and the very process drained you of resources.<br /> <br /> You either give up, or at least give up on the more extreme &quot;solutions&quot;, or whomever caused the Forced Disappearance will have time on their side and probably more.<br /> <br /> Of course, it may be in the end that they just don't expect you to be a total psychopath and bring them down together with two city blocks and a bio hazard that will stay area for generations to come, but at this point they may not be the worst monsters in town anyway...<br /> <br /> And Forced Disappearance is really about using state clot. Things like the disappearance being done by the police and the entire system that should supposedly guard your rights is actually built in this case to hinder your investigation as much as possible. I do think that sometimes, especially for Mages, the Union is just kidnapping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T20:07:00-07:00","id":1466859,"title":"","content":"One thing you have to keep in mind is that the Technocracy actively uses government agencies to cover their actions. An attack on a Tradition Chantry? To the Sleepers it's an FBI raid on a drug cartel hideout or a cult compound. A Mage gets snatched up by some MiBs? A criminal arrested by police.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is really only going to do a forced disappearance if the need to apprehend the target trumps the time needed to set up a proper cover or the target is someone that's not going to be missed or noticed by the public at large. Like an Orphan living on the street getting snatched isn't going to cause much notice while a more high profile target will require creating a cover story to explain their apprehension.<br /> <br /> Another alternative is the Technocracy's cloning ability and simply replacing the target or faking their death so the public never realizes they are missing.<br /> <br /> It's similar to when they recruit a newly Awakened, they create the story of them getting a job or a scholarship that will require them to move away. Which isn't that much of a stretch as they have plenty of Constructs within universities, laboratories, government buildings and the like.<br /> <br /> And that's something they've been doing for a long time so they're pretty good at it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T05:52:44-07:00","id":1466930,"title":"","content":"The only problem with investigating forced disappearances is they probably leave behind a genetically identical clone with a crappy copy of their personality.<br /> <br /> Like Changeling: The Lost.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T11:08:16-07:00","id":1466962,"title":"","content":"Clones are pretty easy for other mages to figure out, esp. since you generally aren't going to get a clone to Awaken, and it will lack all sorts of magical safe guards.<br /> <br /> Cloning is also one of those things that the Technocracy can do, but can't necessarily always do in the moment (or is going to be willing to do for that matter). Creating something as convincing as a Fetch is not a small feat. It's way too much work for Sleeper targets (you can just brainwash them when you're done), and a big outlay of resources against mage and other RD targets that are likely to catch on pretty quick.<br /> <br /> Now.. trying to slide an infiltration operative in.... that's a different story. But again, those don't grow on trees and are going to be for very specific circumstances.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T11:43:11-07:00","id":1466965,"title":"","content":"Also, if you're leaving a clone you're not technically doing a Forced Disappearance, just an old fashioned kidnapping.<br /> <br /> The concept of the Forced Disappearance is about the government doing it. The Union isn't the government, no matter how much control they may have on it. If they're going to leave a clone, why the fuck would they go through all the trouble of doing this kidnapping through governmental channels?<br /> <br /> Why use the system, leaving traces of your activity on the system, if at the end you're going to fool the system anyway? This is kind of counterproductive to say the least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}